"answer": "To confirm a diagnosis of soft tissue sarcoma, doctors use a biopsy [MLP-495]. A biopsy is a procedure that removes cells or tissue to be examined under a microscope, and it is often the only test that can definitively determine if an area is cancer [MLP-5921]. Regarding volcanic eruptions, the groups most at risk for lung damage from gas and ash are small infants, older adults, and people with severe respiratory illnesses [MLP-4600]."
